Owned client setup
Project location: launcher/ and account-runtime/ in this source bundle.

The bundled APK is an unconfigured diagnostic loader. Set up account imports its pinned runtime and offers Sign in or Runtime settings/Self-Check. Launch test app is blocked until the owner supplies a registered test client.

Build the host with JDK 17 and Android SDK 35, the project's existing NDK/toolchain, and an installed owned test APK on the Android device:
  gradle --no-daemon policyChecks :app:assembleDebug \
    -PownedTestPackage=YOUR.OWNED.PACKAGE \
    -PownedTestSha256=ACTUAL_REGISTERED_SIGNER_SHA256 \
    -PownedTestRegistered=true

The package and certificate must describe your APK, and Google Cloud/Play Games registration must use its actual package and signing SHA-1. The registered flag is a declaration; this project cannot verify Google Cloud registration from that flag. Configure any required server/web OAuth client inside your owned app. Do not substitute a third-party package or certificate.

Configure SDK paths in each project's local.properties. Run ./run-checks.sh with JAVA_HOME set to your JDK. The host signing configuration uses the local development key if present; otherwise Android's standard debug key. Private signing keys are excluded from this source bundle. The prebuilt bundled runtime retains its audited development signer and SHA-256 pin.

Runtime source build: Gradle 8.13, JDK 17, Android SDK 36 and the existing dependencies/toolchain; set GRADLE_MICROG_VERSION_WITHOUT_GIT=1 and run :play-services-core:assembleDefaultRelease -Pabi=arm64-v8a. If rebuilding/signing the runtime, recompute BUNDLED_VERSION, BUNDLED_SIZE and BUNDLED_SHA256 in MicrogTrustPolicy before bundling it. Never re-sign the owned test APK to match this runtime.

Test on a device: inspect Diagnostics, complete genuine Google account login in the runtime, verify persistence after restart, grant account visibility through the runtime's normal user-consent UI if required, launch the registered owned APK, and complete its actual Google OAuth/Play Games flow. A created/resumed activity, account presence, anonymous HEAD response or API availability result is not login success.
